==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/laɪnd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-lined.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪnd|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having a [[lining]], an inner [[layer]] or [[covering]].
#: ''Fred liked fully '''lined''' trousers with his suits.''
# {{context|of paper|lang=en}} Having lines, [[ruled]].
#: ''For handwritten work Fred preferred '''lined''' paper to plain.''
# {{context|of skin|lang=en}} Having visible lines or [[wrinkle]]s.
#:* '''1859''', [[w:Charles Dickens|Charles Dickens]], ''[[s:A Tale of Two Cities|A Tale of Two Cities]]'', Book I, ch 4
#:*: He had a healthy colour in his cheeks, and his face, though '''lined''', bore few traces of anxiety.

